From f69db943e6b1b097dc5f6b38154c34c0c8508f72 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 14:53:36 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 27/60] Server: a stream that has not sent its first token gets
 keepalives every TF_SSE_KEEPALIVE_S seconds (default 15).

Queueing and a long prefill send nothing after the head, and clients or proxies
that time out a silent body leave and retry from zero. Chat, completions and
responses streams get an SSE comment (": keepalive"); Anthropic streams get its
ping event. A keepalive that cannot be written cancels the request as a client
that left.

(cherry picked from commit 9fbc2b3edc2e772d28124dfea2da0a0be554de86)
